  "query_preview": "..\nWEATHER PATTERN OVERVIEW:\nA strong upper low over western Montana is expected to be over\nsouthern Sask tonight. Showers with heavy rain and scattered\nthunderstorms moved N-NE through the CWA this morning. An intense\nline of showers/storms were moving east between Billings and\nJordan producing wind gusts to 63 mph (Winnett). This line is\nexpected to move east for a few more hours but will quickly fall\napart when the diurnal heating begins to wane.\n\nWrap-around rain will move east into north-central Montana this\nevening that will move into the CWA Tuesday as an upper\ndisturbance aids in the instability.\n\nThings quiet down a bit for Wednesday with sunshine and\ntemperatures rebound to near normal, mid 70s to near 80 for the\nCWA.\n\nOn Thursday, the next disturbance moves east from western Canada\nwith a cold front approaching the CWA. Temps should reach near 80\nacross the northern zones and possibly near 90 in the southeast\nzones. With Min RH in the teens and an increasing West wind, fire\nweather highlights may need to be considered.\n\nEnsembles then show a much cooler period expected starting Friday\nwith shower chances increasing. Look for high temps to drop into\nthe 60s, possibly 50s if steadier rainshowers occur over the\nweekend.\n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS:\nPops were tweaked toward current conditions and CAMs for the\nremainder of the afternoon. Winds tonight and Tuesday were\ngenerally left untouched as NBM90 wasn't too far off from NBM.\n\nHigh confidence on rain this morning with diminishing confidence\nfor rain this afternoon. High confidence for strong west winds\nthis afternoon, tonight and Tuesday. Tweaked pops early this \nmorning. No other changes at this time. TFJ",
